    apply: "Examine your goals for the next year and ask how each serves others. Release one ambition driven by status. Seek a role in which you serve behind the scenes. Pray Mark 10:45 over your leadership. Memorise Mark 10:43-44.",
    activity: "Read Mark 10:32-45 and list what the disciples wanted and what Jesus taught. Draw two columns for worldly and kingdom greatness. Discuss examples. Pray for humility.",
    takeHome: "Read Mark 9:30-37, Mark 10:32-45, Matthew 20:17-28 and Matthew 23. Write a personal definition of greatness. Memorise Mark 10:43-44.",
    prayer: "Thank Jesus for giving his life for us. Confess our desire for status. Ask for a servant's heart.",
    teacher: "Avoid mocking James and John; they later drank the cup. Be gentle with learners who are ambitious. Help them redirect ambition toward service. Be aware of cultures where titles carry great weight and discuss respectfully.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners how Jesus defines greatness.",
    mcq1: ["What does Mark 10:43 say?", ["Whoever would be great among you must be your servant", "Whoever would be great must rule", "Greatness is wealth", "Greatness is fame"], 0, "The great one is a servant."],
